# Auto-commit & push all affected repos

This workspace is several independent git repos (not a monorepo):
`closet-dashboard`, `custom-closets-websites`, `closet-widget`,
`closet-scraper`, `basic-closet-demo`. Each has its own `origin` and most
auto-deploy to Vercel on push to `main`.

After you finish a task that edits files, commit and push WITHOUT waiting to be
asked again — the user has standing approval for this workspace:

1. For EVERY repo whose working tree changed, run `git add -A` then commit with
   a concise Conventional Commits message (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, etc.)
   describing the "why".
2. Push each committed repo: `git push origin main` (or `git push -u origin main`
   if no upstream). Pushing auto-deploys, so this is the deploy step.
3. If multiple repos changed, commit + push each one separately.
4. Briefly report each commit hash and confirm the push/deploy.

## Guardrails

- Never commit secrets (`.env`, `.env.local`, credentials). They are gitignored
  here — keep them that way; warn instead of committing if one appears.
- Never `git config`, force-push, amend pushed commits, or skip hooks unless the
  user explicitly asks.
- If a push fails (missing remote/auth), report it; don't silently skip.
- If a DB migration was added under `supabase/migrations/`, apply it
  (`bash scripts/db-migrate.sh`) before pushing the code that depends on it.
